<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title><%= title %> · Schematic</title>
  <script>try { document.documentElement.dataset.theme = localStorage.getItem('schema-theme') || (matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme: dark)').matches ? 'dark' : 'light'); } catch { /* Default light. */ }</script>
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com"><link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@400;500;600;700&display=swap">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/style.css?v=<%= locals.assetVersion || '' %>">
  <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/img/favicon.svg">
  <meta name="csrf-token" content="<%= typeof csrfToken !== 'undefined' ? csrfToken : '' %>">
  <script src="/js/auth.js?v=<%= locals.assetVersion || '' %>"></script>
</head>
<body>
<div class="app-shell">
  <aside class="sidebar">
    <div class="sidebar-brand"><img src="/img/favicon.svg" class="logo-mark" alt=""><span>Schematic</span></div>
    <button class="btn btn-primary btn-block" id="add-site"><svg class="nav-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg>Add site</button>
    <div class="sidebar-section"><span>Sites</span><span id="site-count" class="count-pill">0</span></div>
    <nav id="site-list" class="site-list" aria-label="Sites"><p class="muted">Loading sites…</p></nav>
    <div class="sidebar-footer">
      <button class="nav-item" id="open-ai-settings"><svg class="nav-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 3l1.9 4.6L18.5 9.5l-4.6 1.9L12 16l-1.9-4.6L5.5 9.5l4.6-1.9z"/><path d="M19 15l.8 1.9 1.9.8-1.9.8L19 20.4l-.8-1.9-1.9-.8 1.9-.8z"/></svg>AI Settings</button>
      <a class="nav-item" href="/api/workspaces/connector" download><svg class="nav-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 4v11m0 0l-4-4m4 4l4-4M5 20h14"/></svg>Download plugin</a>
      <button class="nav-item" id="open-help"><svg class="nav-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/><path d="M9.5 9.5a2.5 2.5 0 1 1 3.5 2.3c-.6.3-1 .9-1 1.6v.6M12 17.5h.01"/></svg>How it works</button>
      <button class="nav-item theme-toggle" id="theme-toggle" title="Switch light/dark mode"><svg class="nav-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path class="moon" d="M20 14.5A8 8 0 0 1 9.5 4a8 8 0 1 0 10.5 10.5z"/><g class="sun"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="4"/><path d="M12 2v2M12 20v2M4.9 4.9l1.4 1.4M17.7 17.7l1.4 1.4M2 12h2M20 12h2M4.9 19.1l1.4-1.4M17.7 6.3l1.4-1.4"/></g></svg><span class="label">Dark mode</span></button>
      <% if (typeof currentUser !== 'undefined' && currentUser) { %>
      <form method="post" action="/logout" class="sidebar-user">
        <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrfToken %>">
        <span class="user-avatar"><%= String(currentUser).slice(0, 1).toUpperCase() %></span>
        <span class="user-name"><%= currentUser %></span>
        <button class="icon-button" type="submit" title="Sign out" aria-label="Sign out"><svg class="nav-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M15 4h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v12a2 2 0 0 1-2 2h-3M10 8l-4 4 4 4M6 12h10"/></svg></button>
      </form>
      <% } %>
    </div>
  </aside>

  <dialog id="help-dialog" class="site-dialog help-dialog">
    <div class="dialog-body">
      <div class="dialog-heading">
        <div><span class="eyebrow">Guide</span><h2>How Schematic works</h2></div>
        <button type="button" class="icon-button" id="close-help" aria-label="Close">×</button>
      </div>
      <p>Schematic reads your WordPress pages, builds JSON-LD schema for them from your business profile and page rules or with AI, and puts it on the live site through Rank Math. You review everything before it goes live, any change can be undone, and every version is backed up.</p>

      <h3>Before you start (once per site)</h3>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Add site</strong>: the WordPress address, a username and an <strong>Application Password</strong> (WordPress → Users → Profile → Application Passwords). A user with the Editor role is enough.</li>
        <li><strong>Download plugin</strong> and install the <strong>Schematic Connector</strong> on that WordPress site, then click <strong>Test connection</strong>.</li>
        <li><strong>Business profile</strong> (on the site page): it fills itself in from the site. Check the name, phone, address, logo, hours and service areas and save. Every page links to these details. <strong>Page rules</strong> in the same window set which schema each kind of page gets.</li>
        <li><strong>AI Settings</strong>, to use AI. Save an OpenAI or Gemini key; the start and end of the saved key are shown so you can tell keys apart.</li>
      </ol>

      <h3>The five steps</h3>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Crawl</strong>: click <strong>Crawl site</strong>. Schematic reads the site's published pages and lists them. If a firewall blocks a page, it is read through WordPress instead. <strong>Resume / retry pages</strong> finishes anything left unread. To work on just a few pages, open <em>Only specific pages</em>.</li>
        <li><strong>Choose</strong>: tick the pages you want and pick how to build the schema. <strong>Rules</strong> uses your business profile and page rules, with names, FAQs and details copied exactly from each page. <strong>AI</strong> writes it from each page's content in any schema.org types. Tick types and click <strong>Use these types for the ticked pages</strong>, or use <strong>Types</strong> on a row for one page.</li>
        <li><strong>Generate</strong>: click <strong>Generate schema</strong>. When it finishes you are taken to Review.</li>
        <li><strong>Review</strong>: click <strong>Compare</strong> on a page to see the schema on the live site now next to the new schema. Removed lines are red and added lines green. Untick anything you don't want to publish.</li>
        <li><strong>Publish</strong>: click <strong>Publish to site</strong>. Each ticked page's current schema (Rank Math's) is replaced with the new schema and the live page is checked. <strong>Undo last publish</strong> puts the previous schema back.</li>
      </ol>
      <p class="muted">Every step can be opened from the tabs at any time. Opening an earlier run from <strong>Run history</strong> takes you to its Review step, so schema you generated before can be published straight away.</p>

      <h3>Using a header code plugin instead</h3>
      <p>In the Publish step, open <em>Use a header code plugin instead</em> and <strong>Download &lt;script&gt; tags</strong> or <strong>Download JSON</strong> for the checked pages, or open <strong>Compare</strong> on a row and use <strong>Copy &lt;script&gt; tag</strong>. Paste it into WPCode, Insert Headers and Footers or a similar plugin. Don't also apply it with Schematic, or the page will carry it twice.</p>

      <h3>Backups and history</h3>
      <p>Every page's original schema, each generated version, and every publish, removal and undo is saved on the server. <strong>Download all backups</strong> (Publish step, under <em>Use a header code plugin instead</em>) gets them in one file. <strong>Run history</strong> at the bottom of a site lets you reopen any earlier run.</p>

      <h3>Good to know</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Pages whose canonical URL points to another page start unchecked: search engines ignore schema there.</li>
        <li>The business profile card shows anything missing that Google needs for local results (like a full street address) and what is worth adding.</li>
        <li>Every Service lists only the area its page is about (the city in the page title or heading, otherwise the business's own city), never the whole service-area list.</li>
        <li>Opening hours from the business profile are on every page, and are required on service-area pages: those can't be published without them.</li>
        <li>Statuses: <span class="status-dot generated">Schema ready</span> <span class="status-dot published">Published</span> <span class="status-dot generating">Generating</span> <span class="status-dot failed">Failed</span>. The reason for a failure is shown under it and in Compare.</li>
      </ul>

      <div class="dialog-actions"><button type="button" class="btn btn-primary" id="close-help-footer">Got it</button></div>
    </div>
  </dialog>

  <main class="main">
    <div class="main-inner">
